# Why Do We Need Algorithmic Historiography?

**Authors:** Garfield, Eugene, Pudovkin, A. I., Istomin, V. S.

## Abstract
Provides an applications-oriented view of algorithmic historiography and how it relates to understanding scientific paradigms. Discusses HistCite[TM], a program that allows scholars to identify significant works on a given topic; paradigm shifts; a genealogic approach; citation analyses; correcting variations in citations; and bibliographic coupling. (Author/LRW)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ671867

